{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>No man shall stand against you, etc.</b> I know only a man; a nation, a family, and a woman with her witchcraft — from where? Scripture teaches: ״לֹא יִתְיַצֵּב״ in every case. If so, what does Scripture teach by ״אִישׁ״? Even like Og king of Bashan (ibid.)." "<b>Your dread and your fear.</b> But is dread not the same as fear? Rather: your dread upon those nearby, and your fear upon those far off. פַּחַד is a term of sudden alarm; מוֹרָא is a term of prolonged anxiety." "<b>As He spoke to you.</b> And where did He speak? (Exodus 23) ״I will send My terror before you, etc.״ (Sifrei ad loc.)"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:38.928272257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}